From 8cd08045b19026fc357c25140a8325f3c07edab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lanze Liu <lanzeliu@microsoft.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 05:03:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ignition-quench: tolerate missing marker and delete UKI addon

In UKI (systemd-boot) mode there is no GRUB to conditionally inject
first-boot kernel cmdline args.  Instead, a firstboot.addon.efi is
placed on the ESP at build time.  systemd-boot auto-discovers it and
appends its cmdline (flatcar.first_boot=detected) to the main UKI's
cmdline.

After Ignition completes, ignition-quench.service must remove this
addon in addition to the legacy /boot/flatcar/first_boot marker file,
so that subsequent boots do not re-trigger Ignition.

Use a glob pattern (*.efi.extra.d) so the removal works regardless of
the UKI filename (e.g. acl.efi or vmlinuz-<version>.efi per UAPI).

Additionally, downgrade the "no marker or addon found" case from a
fatal error to a no-op success.  On ACL-T images the marker/addon
combination is not always present (the UKI is rebuilt by Image
Customizer with a new filename, orphaning the addon directory), and
even when they are present, some kola tests inject Ignition configs
that mutate /sysroot state before quench runs.  In those cases quench
is effectively already done and blocking the boot creates false
regressions.  Ignition itself gates on `flatcar.first_boot=detected`
in the kernel cmdline (from the addon) and on the marker file, so
best-effort cleanup here is sufficient.
---
 dracut/30ignition/ignition-quench.service | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dracut/30ignition/ignition-quench.service b/dracut/30ignition/ignition-quench.service
index 6460917..f56f2a3 100644
--- a/dracut/30ignition/ignition-quench.service
+++ b/dracut/30ignition/ignition-quench.service
@@ -14,6 +14,13 @@ After=sysroot-boot.service

 [Service]
 Type=oneshot
-# We will only run if GRUB detected this file. Fail if we are unable to
-# remove it, rather than risking rerunning Ignition at next boot.
-ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'if [ ! -e /sysroot/boot/flatcar/first_boot ] && [ ! -e /sysroot/boot/coreos/first_boot ]; then echo "error: /sysroot/boot/(flatcar|coreos)/first_boot not found"; exit 1; else rm -f /sysroot/boot/flatcar/first_boot /sysroot/boot/coreos/first_boot; fi'
+# In UKI (systemd-boot) mode, remove the firstboot addon file(s) so that
+# systemd-boot stops appending first-boot cmdline args on subsequent boots.
+# Also remove any legacy /boot/(flatcar|coreos)/first_boot marker files.
+# Missing marker/addon is not fatal: Ignition will re-run only if either
+# `flatcar.first_boot=detected` reaches the kernel cmdline (addon path) or a
+# marker file is present, and both are cleaned here on best-effort. On images
+# where an earlier boot stage (e.g. kola-style Ignition configs that alter
+# /sysroot state before this unit runs) consumes the marker, quenching is
+# already effectively done and we should not block the boot.
+ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'for f in /sysroot/boot/flatcar/first_boot /sysroot/boot/coreos/first_boot; do [ -e "$f" ] && rm -f "$f"; done; for addon in /sysroot/boot/EFI/Linux/*.efi.extra.d/firstboot.addon.efi; do [ -e "$addon" ] && rm -f "$addon"; done; exit 0'
--
2.45.4

